MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze felt like a natural next choice after Old Sock because I wanted more of that relaxed, blues-rooted listening mood.",
    "In My Soul and Don't Explain matched the soulful side of my interest in Memphis, while Gary Clark Jr. Live connected with the electric blues guitar appeal of People, Hell & Angels."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Wallflower's polished vocal direction did not fit the blues and roots rock I wanted today, even if it might appeal on another visit.",
    "Reworked duets were not especially compelling to me today, and An Anthology gave me too little indication of a specific sound to make me want to investigate."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The suggestions seemed to treat a broad connection to blues and roots music as enough, although relaxed blues, electric guitar, and polished vocals appeal to me differently.",
    "Several live and acoustic recordings were plausible matches, but those formats alone did not give me a stronger reason to choose them."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The particular connection to Old Sock mattered most today: I wanted the relaxed blues-rooted direction that drew me to The Breeze.",
    "Finding several albums appealing does not mean I want several now; I rarely choose anything unless one album gives me a clear reason to listen."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in blues, soul, and roots rock, but only The Breeze matched the particular mood strongly enough for me to choose it today."
}
